```

`offset` and `size` are 32-bit values. `buf_offset + eocd_offset` is the absolute position of the EOCD record. The check ensures the central directory doesn't extend past the EOCD record.

But what if `offset` is 0 and `size` is very large? Then `offset + size` could overflow (but the overflow check catches this). If it doesn't overflow, `offset + size > buf_offset + eocd_offset` would be true (since `buf_offset + eocd_offset` is the position of the EOCD record near the end of the file), and the function returns NULL.

